{number: 114}
{title: Mine Eyes Have Seen the Glory}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Mine [Bb] eyes have seen the glory of the coming of the Lord;
He is [Eb] trampling out the vintage where the [Bb] grapes of wrath are stored;
He hath [Bb] loosed the fateful lightning of His [Gm] terrible swift sword:
His [Cm] truth is [F7] marching [Bb] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bb] Glory, glory, hallelujah!
[Eb] Glory, glory, halle-[Bb] lujah!
[Bb] Glory, glory, [Gm] hallelujah!
His [Cm] truth is [F7] marching [Bb] on.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I have [Bb] seen Him in the watchfires of a hundred circling camps;
They have [Eb] builded Him an altar in the [Bb] evening dews and damps;
I can [Bb] read His righteous sentence by the [Gm] dim and flaring lamps:
His [Cm] day is [F7] marching [Bb] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
In the [Bb] beauty of the lilies Christ was born across the sea,
With a [Eb] glory in His bosom that trans-[Bb] figures you and me:
As He [Bb] died to make men holy, let us [Gm] live to make men free,
While [Cm] God is [F7] marching [Bb] on.
{end_of_verse}
